# Dunots Mobile workflow

- Implement requested mobile changes directly; do not wait for the user to copy code manually.
- Keep mobile and desktop changes separate.
- Preserve the dependency order: leaf files, feature screens, shell, app configuration, entry point.
- Keep tests under test/ and production code under lib/.
- Run formatting, static analysis, tests, and builds appropriate to the change.
- Fix blocking validation errors before reporting completion.
- Do not create commits or push. Provide granular Git commands for the user.
- Separate commits by responsibility and never include unrelated desktop changes.
- Update docs/plan.md, docs/checks.md, or docs/decisions.md when the project direction changes.